<title>USA: Alpha-based PCs to use Ramtron technology.</title>
<headline>Alpha-based PCs to use Ramtron technology.</headline>
<dateline>COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ramtron International Corp on Monday said its memory technology will be used in personal computers running on Digital Equipment Corp's Alpha microprocessor and VLSI Technology Inc's Polaris chipset.</p>
<p>Ramtron said its high sustained bandwidth Enhanced Synchronous DRAM, or ESDRAM, memory will boost the performance lead of Alpha-based personal computers operating under heavy Windows NT workloads.</p>
<p>Ramtron said ESDRAM was developed by Ramtron's Enhanced Memory Systems Inc unit.</p>
<p>((Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
